{
 "uid": "utm-obs-04-ceph",
 "title": "04 - Ceph & Storage Health",
 "description": "**Purpose:** first-class storage-infrastructure dashboard. Ceph underpins every stateful UTM workload; storage degradation surfaces as unexplained application failures.\n\n**Data sources:** Prometheus scraping `rook-ceph-mgr:9283` (412 ceph_* metrics), plus kubelet volume stats for PVCs.\n\n**IMPORTANT — this required an infrastructure fix.** Before this work, Prometheus held ZERO `ceph_*` metrics: rook-ceph-mgr served them but no ServiceMonitor existed in the `rook-ceph` namespace (all 17 ServiceMonitors were in `monitoring`). A ServiceMonitor was added — no new exporter was deployed.\n\n**Known limitation:** per-OSD byte utilisation is not exposed by ceph-mgr. See the gap panel.\n\n**Why this matters operationally:** HDD-backed OSDs + node disks above 80% produce BlueStore slow ops, which time out Kubernetes liveness probes and cause cluster-wide restart storms.",
 "tags": [
  "utm-observability",
  "ceph",
  "storage"
 ],
 "timezone": "browser",
 "editable": true,
 "graphTooltip": 1,
 "schemaVersion": 41,
 "version": 0,
 "weekStart": "",
 "refresh": "30s",
 "preload": false,
