    },
    "content": "### Per-OSD capacity is NOT available\n\n`rook-ceph-mgr` (port 9283) exposes OSD **state** (`ceph_osd_up`, `ceph_osd_in`, `ceph_osd_weight`) and **latency** (`ceph_osd_apply_latency_ms`, `ceph_osd_commit_latency_ms`), but **not** per-OSD byte utilisation — there is no `ceph_osd_stat_bytes_used` on this endpoint (verified empty).\n\nCapacity on this dashboard is therefore reported at **cluster** and **pool** level, which is accurate but coarser.\n\nTo obtain per-OSD fill levels, either add a ServiceMonitor for `rook-ceph-exporter` (port 9926) or run `ceph osd df` in the toolbox. Not added here to keep the change minimal."
